,title,link,text,language,family
0,Traditional Childhood Songs - The Creole Melting Pot,https://www.thecreolemeltingpot.com/childhood-songs/,"February 18, 2021 - These French songs were introduced to the Seychelles by the French speaking settlers, sailors and traders as well as the Catholic missionaries and the English songs by the British Administrators when the Seychelles was a British colony. Some of these songs were found in a small booklet entitled Le Serin Chanteur .",Seychelles French Creole,Creole
1,Creole Music and Dance Bring the Spirit of Seychelles Alive – Harbinger Standard,https://harbingerstandard.com/seychelles/seychelles-creole-music-and-dance-ignite-spirit/,"August 6, 2025 - Sega music, characterized by its lively tempos and infectious energy, can often be heard during celebrations and gatherings. It originates from the islands’ African roots infused with French and Creole influences, making it a true melting pot of sounds and styles.",Seychelles French Creole,Creole
2,Seychelles latest creole music - YouTube,https://www.youtube.com/playlist?list=PL2DWjL_qbD8hE9PuRrftUiK0NY0Iog_wP,Compilation from Seychelles,Seychelles French Creole,Creole
3,Seychelles - The Creole Melting Pot,https://www.thecreolemeltingpot.com/seychelles/,"July 5, 2021 - Despite the fact that English still remains as the official language of the government and business, Seychellois Creole is considered to be the most widely used language of conversations. All Seychellois communicates in three languages, ie: Kreol, French and English and the Nation local newspaper is always published in the three official languages. Music and dance have always played a prominent role in Seychelles culture and in all types of local festivities.",Seychelles French Creole,Creole
4,Seychelles Creole: Children's Songs and Rhymes - Mama Lisa's World,https://www.mamalisa.com/?t=el&lang=Seychelles+Creole,"Each includes the full text in the original language, with an English translation. Each also features links to recordings on the Mama Lisa website, some by professional musicians, but many by ordinary people who have contributed them to us, to help preserve their culture.",Seychelles French Creole,Creole
5,Festival Kreol In Seychelles: Experience Creole Tradition Through Music And Dance - FunTimes Magazine,https://funtimesmagazine.com/festival-kreol-in-seychelles-experience-creole-tradition-through-music-and-dance/,"November 9, 2025 - A small country with an estimated population of 92,000, Seychelles’ economy is strengthened by its tourism potential and is one of the few African countries that boasts of a high Human Development Index. Creole language, which is a blend of several African languages and French, is one of the National languages. Along with English and French, this blend of cultural mix over the years has brought about a Creole tradition that is expressed through art, music, dance, and poetry and celebrated at the annual Festival Kreol.",Seychelles French Creole,Creole
6,Seychelles Yacht Blog: The Music and Dance of the Seychelles,https://seychellesyacht.blogspot.com/2013/09/the-music-and-dance-of-seychelles.html?m=1,"However, one point on which they have never compromised is their choice of language. All their lyrics are in French Antillean Creole, a local dialect not widely known outside the islands. Seggae Music Even before blending the two sounds, there are obvious similarities between Seychellois music ...",Seychelles French Creole,Creole
7,Music of the Seychelles • Approach Guides,https://approachguides.com/blog/music-of-the-seychelles/,"May 3, 2024 - Their music has become strongly ... acceptance it deserves. Their instrumentation is entirely traditional and includes African instruments such as the djembe, the doumdoum, the balafon and the bobre....",Seychelles French Creole,Creole
8,Festival Kreol 2025: Celebrate Creole Music on the Seychelles in October,https://maarcofrancis.com/attractions-and-landmarks/2025-seychelles-creole-music-festival/,"August 22, 2025 - The World Creole Music Festival is back in 2025, inviting music lovers to experience three days of vibrant Creole culture in the beautiful Seychelles.",Seychelles French Creole,Creole
9,"Audio Recording, Songs, Creole, Music | Library of Congress","https://loc.gov/audio/?all=true&c=100&fa=subject:songs,+creole|subject:music","Music lontan Catalog Record Only Sung in French Créole of Réunion, with brass instrumental accompaniment. ""Les cuivres de la Réunion."" Production level cataloging. ... Seychelles liberation 82 Catalog Record Only Title on container: Seychelles liberasyon 82. On container: Seychelles laniverser 5an. Production level cataloging. ... Allons boire un coup a collection of Cajun and Creole drinking songs.",Seychelles French Creole,Creole
